hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16744","He said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Ali narrated to us, from Yahya, meaning Ibn Abi Kathir, he said: Hayya al-Tamimi narrated to me that his father informed him that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is nothing in ham, and the eye is true, and the truest of omens is the good omen."
"16745","He said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Aban and Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Jafar, from Ata ibn Yasar, from some of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: While a man was praying trailing his izar, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Go and perform wudu; he said: So he went and performed wudu, then came; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Go and perform wudu; he said: So he went and performed wudu, then came; and he said: What is with you, O Messenger of Allah, why did you order him to perform wudu then fall silent; he said: He was praying trailing his izar, and Allah, mighty and majestic, does not accept the prayer of a servant trailing his izar."
